# FORMSHIFT AI — COMPLETE MASTER IMPLEMENTATION SPECIFICATION

## 1. PROJECT OVERVIEW

Project name: FormShift AI

Project type: Premium multi-brand automotive discovery, 3D vehicle customization, customer inquiry management, and CRM automation platform.

Primary objective: Build a polished, interactive automotive web application where users can explore different car brands, inspect vehicle details, customize supported vehicle features in 3D, save their configurations, and submit inquiries. The business team will manage those inquiries through an internal CRM supported by reliable workflow automation.

The application should demonstrate advanced frontend engineering, interactive 3D rendering, database design, authentication, secure APIs, CRM development, AI integration, automation workflows, and production deployment.

This is an independent automotive configurator concept, not an official manufacturer website, dealership, or vehicle-ordering service.

The system must distinguish between:
- Verified vehicle specifications.
- Illustrative or estimated prices.
- User-selected configurations.
- Actual customer inquiries.
- Internal sales opportunities.
- Completed sales, which must never be fabricated.

Do not imply an official relationship with Tesla, Bugatti, Lamborghini, or any other manufacturer without authorization.

## 2. CORE PRODUCT VISION

FormShift AI has two main experiences.

### A. Customer-facing automotive experience

Visitors can:
- Explore supported car brands.
- Browse available vehicles.
- Search and filter the catalog.
- View vehicle specifications and gallery images.
- Open an interactive 3D configurator.
- Customize supported exterior paint, wheels, trim, and accessories.
- View a summary of their selected options.
- See indicative pricing when reliable pricing data is available.
- Save and restore configurations.
- Compare vehicles using available specifications.
- Ask an AI assistant for recommendations.
- Submit a vehicle inquiry with their chosen configuration.
- Receive a confirmation when the inquiry is successfully saved.

### B. Internal business and CRM experience

Authorized staff can:
- View inquiries submitted by customers.
- Manage contact records and leads.
- Review the selected vehicle and configuration.
- Assign leads to salespeople.
- Create and manage sales opportunities.
- Update pipeline stages.
- Record notes and activities.
- Schedule follow-up tasks.
- Monitor customer communications.
- View automation execution history.
- Investigate failed integrations and retry eligible operations.
- Review dashboard metrics calculated from real database data.

The customer experience and the internal CRM must be integrated through a consistent data model.

